  "description": "## What's New in v6.7.0\n\n### Fixed\n- The message-count sliding window (MaxMessageCount) can no longer drop the anchoring user message. Long agentic runs (RunAgentAsync/RunAgentStreamAsync) append two messages per tool round and could push the originating user query out of the window, producing requests with no user message that some OpenAI-compatible servers reject (e.g. vLLM/Qwen 400 \"No user query found in messages\"). The window now re-anchors the most recent cut-off user message whenever the sliced window has no user turn.\n\n### Deprecated\n- AIService.MaxMessageCount is now [Obsolete] and will be removed in v7.0 — context management becomes token-based only (ConversationPolicy). Until then the window is guaranteed to preserve the most recent user message.\n\nRequires Mythosia.AI.Abstractions v2.4.0.\n\n---\n\n## Documentation\n- Basic Usage: https://github.com/AJ-comp/Mythosia.AI/wiki\n- Advanced Features: https://github.com/AJ-comp/Mythosia.AI/wiki/Advanced-Features\n- Release Notes: https://github.com/AJ-comp/Mythosia.AI/wiki/Release-Notes\n- GitHub: https://github.com/AJ-comp/Mythosia.AI",
